{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 4.5% a year from $70.3 billion in FY2016 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F205], but the path was a step change, not a straight line."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue jumped 19.8% in FY2020 and 13.3% in FY2021 [D183][D230], then fell 1.6%, 0.8% and 1.7% in FY2023 through FY2025 [D324][D370][D416]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 step came from a 19.3% comparable sales increase as the pandemic shifted spending toward the stores [P51][P55]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The recent decline reflects a 2.6% comparable sales decrease in FY2025, split between 2.2% lower traffic and 0.4% lower average transaction [P14]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Merchandise sales are 98.0% of revenue in FY2025 [D465], so the category mix inside that line is the whole growth story."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Food & beverage grew to 23.0% of revenue in FY2025 from 19.6% in FY2017 [D484][D506], adding 0.3pp of growth in FY2025 while apparel fell 4.7% and subtracted 0.7pp [D508][D564][D565]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The filings attribute the FY2023 sales decline to weakness in discretionary categories, partly offset by frequency categories [P30], and that mix shift has persisted."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew only 0.6% a year over the window against 4.5% revenue growth [F207][F205], so there was no operating leverage across the decade."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "EPS diluted compounded at 6.3% against 3.4% net income growth [F210][F208], as diluted shares fell from 582.5 million to 455.6 million [X107][X116]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin was 4.9% in FY2025 [F34], below the 5.6% window median [D590] and far under the 8.4% FY2021 high [D589]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 margin fell 0.3pp [D429], with cost of revenue taking 0.3pp and SG&A adding 0.1pp [D440][D441]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The gross margin rate slipped to 27.9% from 28.2% [P12], while the SG&A rate held at 20.6% only because of a 0.6pp interchange settlement benefit [P11]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The largest move was FY2022, when operating margin fell 4.9pp [D290] as cost of revenue took 4.6pp [D301]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "That year's margin compression came from promotional and clearance markdowns, excess inventory removal and higher supply-chain costs [P38]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow was 1.77x net income in FY2025 [D404], below the 2.01x window median [D619], and free cash flow was 0.77x net income [D405]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 operating cash flow decline reflects lower net earnings and lower accounts payable leverage [P7]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin was 2.7% in FY2025 [D401], under the 4.5% window median [D596] and the 4.2% retail peer median [D611]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex was 3.6% of revenue and 1.19x D&A in FY2025 [D400][D406], up from 2.7% of revenue in FY2024 [D354]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The capex increase reflects more spending on new stores and remodels [P5], and management guides to about $5 billion in FY2026 [P4]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash was $5.49 billion against $14.4 billion of long-term debt in FY2025 [F144][F194], leaving the company in net debt."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio was 0.94x [F184], equal to the 0.94x window median [D602] and above the 0.83x FY2018 low [D600]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity was 24.0% [D415], below the 28.6% retail peer median [D617]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $2.46 billion were 86.8% of free cash flow in FY2025 [D412][D413], and the diluted share count fell 1.3% [D434]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue has fallen three years running, from $109.1 billion in FY2022 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [R1][F7][F10], a 1.3% three-year CAGR [D603]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The decline is traffic-led, with FY2025 comparable sales down 2.6% on a 2.2% traffic drop [P14], which matters because it erodes fixed-cost leverage."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio sits at 0.94x [R2][F184], meaning current liabilities of $21.2 billion exceed current assets of $20.0 billion [F164][F154]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin has fallen two years in a row, 0.4pp in total, to 4.9% [R4][F32][F34]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Data-quality note: short-term investments are already inside cash [R7][F144][X170], and the FY2016-FY2018 current debt portion is inside long-term debt [R8][X177][X173], so net-cash figures are excluded here."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin: a print below the 4.9% FY2025 level [F34] would extend the two-year slide, while a recovery above the 5.6% window median [D590] would reverse it; the FY2026 10-K will show it."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin: holding at or above the 4.5% window median [D596] would confirm cash generation, while a drop toward the 2.7% FY2025 level [D401] would not; watch the FY2026 cash flow statement."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex: spending near the guided $5 billion [P4] against FY2025's $3.73 billion [F94] would keep free cash flow under pressure; the FY2026 10-K will report the actual figure."}
  ]}
]}
